    narr:generatedFrom "37b6bf2c84965cc245e031aab2e50ce7a0484a10" ;
    narr:narration """This narrative carries a cutover-sequencing decision for a four-site migration, argued across two meetings and firming rather than reopening. It opens with [the steering-group deadline forcing the shape to be decided](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_1) and [the four sites laid out, one flagged as the one nobody wants to touch](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_5). The mainline lands as [a flat refusal of parallel cutovers, even for the two small ones](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_8), grounded in [contained pain at one desk versus an unbounded double cutover](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_13) and [the rota-versus-compound reframing of the desk's objection](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_15). The soak gets [a two-week number defended from a pilot whose exception queue didn't flatten until day nine or ten](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_19). The second meeting adds the load-bearing new register: [the supervisor arithmetic showing a double cutover would pull eight of eleven supervisors off the floor](narr:Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_11), sharpened into [risk reframed as arithmetic — the constraint that doesn't move](narr:Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_14), plus [a side benefit: the learning curve across sites](narr:Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_18) and [a demand that a soak never be shortened because a date slipped](narr:Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_28). It closes with [the upward summary: one at a time, two-week soak, replica reporting, vendor holds](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_42).""" ;
